# What never belongs in a build context (README section 23).
#
# The context is the repository root, because a service image is built from the parent POM
# and libs/ as well as from its own module. Without this file that context is the build
# outputs too: eleven target directories and a node_modules, several hundred megabytes sent
# to the daemon on every build, and a jar from the host leaking into an image that is
# supposed to have built its own.

# Build outputs. The images build their own; one copied in from a developer's machine would
# make an image that cannot be reproduced.
target/
**/target/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/

# Local state and secrets. .env holds the credentials of a developer's stack and is the one
# file that must never be baked into a layer.
.env
.git/
.github/
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/

# Nothing an image needs.
*.md
docs/
load-tests/
scripts/
deploy/helm/
deploy/k8s/
deploy/grafana/
deploy/prometheus/
deploy/tempo/
**/*.log
